event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0db836c4a0149292016a68eb9428288195b0a8dd225bcea3c5","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":355,"text":"FAIL\n\nASSIGNED-MOMENT VERDICTS  \nprimary-job promise: MATERIAL  \ninstruction: NONE ASSIGNED  \nunassigned passages: OK\n\n### Voice Gap 1: The method promise retreats into disclaimers\n\n**Our passage:** “This method has helped a lot of people, and there is a good chance it can help you too. Results naturally vary, and it might not be entirely easy for everyone, but many readers report finding it easier than they expected.”\n\n**Real passage:** “This book will help you to understand the truth about BAD SUGAR and take you through a proven method to cut it out of your diet completely and permanently, without leaving you feeling deprived or requiring any willpower. In fact, it will be easy.”\n\n**What Carr's voice does here:** Carr tells the reader plainly what the method will do: reveal the truth, remove bad sugar completely and permanently, and do so without deprivation or willpower. The certainty creates earned authority and immediate relief.\n\n**Where our voice fails:** “There is a good chance,” “results naturally vary,” “might not,” and “many readers report” turn the central promise into a cautious testimonial disclaimer. Instead of hearing directly from a trusted guide, the reader hears impersonal, liability-conscious language that leaves the method itself unresolved.\n\n**Initial suspicion (speculative):** writer-prompt — The passage appears to prioritize defensive qualification over the commissioned method promise.\n\n## Final verdict\n\n**Overall voice-effect assessment:** The largest gap is weakened authority at the method promise. The cluster of hedges—especially “there is a good chance,” “results naturally vary,” and “it might not be entirely easy”—creates doubt where the real chapter gives the reader a firm, relieving assurance."}

